# Built artefacts. Reproducible from administrativ's road graph plus scripts/, so they are
# not committed — road_time.parquet alone is one row per adjacent UAT pair.
data/*.parquet
data/reports/

# Small, validated documents under data/*.json stay tracked on purpose: scripts/validate_data.py
# globs simulators/*/data/*.json and checks each against its schema, so ignoring the whole
# directory would quietly remove this simulator from the repository's one data gate.

# data/*.geojson IS tracked, deliberately. The rail geometry is derived — but the pipeline
# that makes it needs a 1 GB OSM extract and therefore does not run in CI, while the app build
# does, and copies these into its bundle. Ignoring them would turn the rail toggle into a
# button that fetches a 404 on the published site, which fails at click time rather than at
# build time. 2,1 MB against 26 MB of headroom in scripts/check_repo_size.py.
